templates.letter1:
{{salutation}}

My name is {{sender_name}}, and I live and work here in the Belmont area. I'm writing because I'm looking to buy a home in your neighborhood, and I wanted to reach out to you directly about {{property_phrase}} before I look elsewhere.

I know a letter like this can arrive out of the blue. Many longtime Belmont homeowners have told me they've thought about what comes next for their home, whether that means downsizing, moving closer to family, or simply not wanting to keep up with repairs and upkeep, but they haven't wanted the hassle of listing it, showing it, and paying commissions. If that sounds at all familiar, I may be able to help.

If you ever decide to sell, here is what I can offer:
- A fair, straightforward offer with no real estate commissions.
- You choose the closing date, whether that's in a few weeks or many months from now.
- No repairs, cleaning, or showings. Leave behind anything you don't want.
- All the time you need to talk it over with your family or your attorney. I'm glad to answer their questions too.

There is no obligation and no pressure. If the timing isn't right, or you have no interest in selling, I understand completely, and if you let me know, you won't hear from me again.

You can reach me directly at {{phone}} or {{email}}. Thank you for reading.

{{closing}}

{{sender_name}}
{{company}}
{{phone}} | {{email}}

P.S. Even if you're only curious what your home might be worth in today's market, I'm happy to share what I'm seeing in Belmont, with no strings attached.

templates.letter2:
{{salutation}}

A few weeks ago I sent you a note about {{property_phrase}}, and I wanted to follow up in case it was set aside or arrived at a busy time.

I'm a local buyer looking for a home in your part of Belmont. If you or your family have thought about selling, now or at some point down the road, I'd welcome a short, no-pressure conversation about what would work for you: your timeline, leaving the house as it is, and avoiding commissions and showings.

If you're not interested, a quick note or call saying so is all it takes, and I won't write again.

You can reach me at {{phone}} or {{email}}. Thank you for your time.

{{closing}}

{{sender_name}}
{{company}}
{{phone}} | {{email}}

